(3067259, 430421, 164, '<td valign="top">clever</td>', 'clever', '2006-11-27 22:43:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067267, 432105, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is a gorgeous flower photo.  Very well done in that regard.  Great control of lighting and the image is very crisp and well focused.  With all of that being said I can''t help but wonder if this is going to get severly dinged for the "white" that you''ve used.  Technically the background flowers are white, but there are other tones mixed in.  Anyway, best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'This is a gorgeous flower photo.  Very well done in that regard.  Great control of lighting and the image is very crisp and well focused.  With all of that being said I can''t help but wonder if this is going to get severly dinged for the "white" that you''ve used.  Technically the background flowers are white, but there are other tones mixed in.  Anyway, best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 22:52:07.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067270, 430266, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is nice.  I like the material you''ve used as the primary subject and the paper/ribbon curls add a very nice touch.  Good use of lighting.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'This is nice.  I like the material you''ve used as the primary subject and the paper/ribbon curls add a very nice touch.  Good use of lighting.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 22:54:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067275, 430748, 66976, '<td valign="top">cute!!!</td>', 'cute!!!', '2006-11-27 22:57:57.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067276, 431931, 30049, '<td valign="top">This is very well thought out, and it''s obvious you''ve invested some time in the setup.  It''s a nice photo overall, should do well as a stock image for you if so inclined.  Something about this seems a little bit off for this challenge.  I think it''s the wrapping paper color.  There''s too much of it and not enough white.  If that bottom package was white I think it would make a big difference in this presentation.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This is very well thought out, and it''s obvious you''ve invested some time in the setup.  It''s a nice photo overall, should do well as a stock image for you if so inclined.  Something about this seems a little bit off for this challenge.  I think it''s the wrapping paper color.  There''s too much of it and not enough white.  If that bottom package was white I think it would make a big difference in this presentation.  All JMO of course.  :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 22:58:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067282, 431398, 30049, '<td valign="top">This location looks VERY familiar.  :D  Could be another lake I guess, but it looks like an image I commented on some time ago last year.  I like this as an entry in this challenge.  Hopefully the majority of viewers will think the greyscale trees are "light" enough.  My only complaint is the title.  The last bit about full-color; really didn''t need that in there.  JMO of course. :D  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This location looks VERY familiar.  :D  Could be another lake I guess, but it looks like an image I commented on some time ago last year.  I like this as an entry in this challenge.  Hopefully the majority of viewers will think the greyscale trees are "light" enough.  My only complaint is the title.  The last bit about full-color; really didn''t need that in there.  JMO of course. :D  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 23:00:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067292, 431751, 66976, '<td valign="top">nicely done...</td>', 'nicely done...', '2006-11-27 23:03:35.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067298, 431640, 30049, '<td valign="top">Why?  Of all the subjects available.  Anyway...  The photo is fine for the challenge in technical terms, although I think the subject matter (lady) takes too much space in your composition.  Lighting seems to be a little too harsh and it makes her far breast look funny (smaller and almost disconnected or floating in air).  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'Why?  Of all the subjects available.  Anyway...  The photo is fine for the challenge in technical terms, although I think the subject matter (lady) takes too much space in your composition.  Lighting seems to be a little too harsh and it makes her far breast look funny (smaller and almost disconnected or floating in air).  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 23:04:55.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067302, 431441, 65858, '<td valign="top">Nice texture - I can almost smell the leather.</td>', 'Nice texture - I can almost smell the leather.', '2006-11-27 23:05:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067305, 431751, 65858, '<td valign="top">Captivating eyes.  Nice shot!</td>', 'Captivating eyes.  Nice shot!', '2006-11-27 23:06:05.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067311, 431906, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like this.  Good use of odd numbered subjects in your composition.  Simple, clean photo.  Nice and crisp...should do ok with this one.  Good luck.</td>', 'I like this.  Good use of odd numbered subjects in your composition.  Simple, clean photo.  Nice and crisp...should do ok with this one.  Good luck.', '2006-11-27 23:07:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067318, 432080, 30049, '<td valign="top">This could have much more potential if the background and rug were true white.  The "color temperature" (white balance) is off - too cold (blue).  Clever idea nonetheless.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'This could have much more potential if the background and rug were true white.  The "color temperature" (white balance) is off - too cold (blue).  Clever idea nonetheless.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-27 23:08:41.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067325, 432017, 50034, '<td valign="top"><b>Thank You for the funny "tongue-in-cheek" approach!</b>  I feel for ya!  <i>Digital is tough to learn, tough to project competence, tough to post-process, and "murder" on tongues...(I have tasted sooooooo much blood trying to become a decent digital photographer!!!!)</i> <br/> <br/>It''s similar to the comments I used to get in high school about <b>my stand-up comedy routines</b>, <i>"Haselton, 10,000 comedians out of work!...And you''re trying to be funny!?!"</i>  Anybody who has read one of my "funny" comments or seen one of my "funny" challenge entries will confirm.  I''m a bit <b>THICK</b>!  <i>I can''t quit!</i>  This challenge is a prime example of that!  <b>See if you can pick me out of the line-up!</b> <br/> <br/>Finally, when I came to DPC last Christmas I was so smug, <i>"I am a GOOD photographer!  Y''all don''t clap!  Just throw 10s &amp; 20s!"</i> <b>WOW!!!!!!!  What a rude awakening!</b>  I have been reduced the the T-Ball League!  Now my thoughts are [i]"Geppeto (alanfreed), I want to be a real boy (photographer!)"  "Whenna you prove-a yousef worthy, thenna you be one!"  "Thank you, O Great One!  Until then I''ll just keep ''whittlin'' on my pixels...  What''s that, Roy?  Somethin'' about whittlin'' pixels &amp; grinnin''?"  (Eeps, sorry!  That''s another show...Hee, Hee, Hee, Hee, Hee, Haw!!!!!!!)</td>', 'Thank You for the funny "tongue-in-cheek" approach!  I feel for ya!  Digital is tough to learn, tough to project competence, tough to post-process, and "murder" on tongues...(I have tasted sooooooo much blood trying to become a decent digital photographer!!!!)  It''s similar to the comments I used to get in high school about my stand-up comedy routines, "Haselton, 10,000 comedians out of work!...And you''re trying to be funny!?!"  Anybody who has read one of my "funny" comments or seen one of my "funny" challenge entries will confirm.  I''m a bit THICK!  I can''t quit!  This challenge is a prime example of that!  See if you can pick me out of the line-up!  Finally, when I came to DPC last Christmas I was so smug, "I am a GOOD photographer!  Y''all don''t clap!  Just throw 10s & 20s!" WOW!!!!!!!  What a rude awakening!  I have been reduced the the T-Ball League!  Now my thoughts are [i]"Geppeto (alanfreed), I want to be a real boy (photographer!)"  "Whenna you prove-a yousef worthy, thenna you be one!"  "Thank you, O Great One!  Until then I''ll just keep ''whittlin'' on my pixels...  What''s that, Roy?  Somethin'' about whittlin'' pixels & grinnin''?"  (Eeps, sorry!  That''s another show...Hee, Hee, Hee, Hee, Hee, Haw!!!!!!!)', '2006-11-27 23:11:15.000000', NULL, 1),
(3067326, 431086, 30049, '<td valign="top">Very, very nice.  Wonderful touch in positioning and in disturbing the sand to indicate some "movement".  Hope this does well for you.  Good luck.</td>', 'Very, very nice.  Wonderful touch in positioning and in disturbing the sand to indicate some "movement".  Hope this does well for you.  Good luck.', '2006-11-27 23:11:28.000000', NULL, 1),
