(3069126, 429501, 66597, '<td valign="top">Although some might find the push pin body too soft, I am not bothered by that, as I assume it was intentional. What doesn''t work so well is that the most vibrant part of this - the metal pin portion- naturally becomes the subject as the eye is drawn to it first. Due to its position, the eye then goes straight out of the photo. I''d like to see this with the pin rotated and the metal tip pointed down into the photo.</td>', 'Although some might find the push pin body too soft, I am not bothered by that, as I assume it was intentional. What doesn''t work so well is that the most vibrant part of this - the metal pin portion- naturally becomes the subject as the eye is drawn to it first. Due to its position, the eye then goes straight out of the photo. I''d like to see this with the pin rotated and the metal tip pointed down into the photo.', '2006-11-28 19:53:00.000000', NULL, 1),
