(3072729, 431156, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like this very much.  I do wish however that the background was a true white instead of grey.  The shadow adds a nice element to the composition.  Lighting may be a little hot - very hard to illuminate shiny surfaces.  Perhaps a diffuser?  Anyway, overall a job well done.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like this very much.  I do wish however that the background was a true white instead of grey.  The shadow adds a nice element to the composition.  Lighting may be a little hot - very hard to illuminate shiny surfaces.  Perhaps a diffuser?  Anyway, overall a job well done.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-29 16:09:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3072735, 431792, 30049, '<td valign="top">I like your selection of aperture here to obtain the DOF that works well here.  The OOF areas are creating some nice bokeh.  I do wish the at least some of the background was a true white rather than greyish.  JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.</td>', 'I like your selection of aperture here to obtain the DOF that works well here.  The OOF areas are creating some nice bokeh.  I do wish the at least some of the background was a true white rather than greyish.  JMO of course.  Good luck in the challenge.', '2006-11-29 16:10:53.000000', NULL, 1),
(3072738, 432076, 30049, '<td valign="top">Cute.  Any other time this would probably do a little better.  In this challenge I think the whites should be more luminous than the subject.  JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Cute.  Any other time this would probably do a little better.  In this challenge I think the whites should be more luminous than the subject.  JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-29 16:12:22.000000', NULL, 1),
(3072750, 431051, 30049, '<td valign="top">Very clever.  :D  Fun too!  Only thing that seems strange from here is the white background is splotchy with an area starting in the top third, over and around the mask, and finishing in the top right, that is a dull flat off-white.  The rest is a true white.  Looks like an area of selection in post-processing perhaps?  Maybe it''s just this cruddy monitor I have to use at the office.  :P  Anyway, best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'Very clever.  :D  Fun too!  Only thing that seems strange from here is the white background is splotchy with an area starting in the top third, over and around the mask, and finishing in the top right, that is a dull flat off-white.  The rest is a true white.  Looks like an area of selection in post-processing perhaps?  Maybe it''s just this cruddy monitor I have to use at the office.  :P  Anyway, best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-29 16:15:48.000000', NULL, 1),
