(3074941, 431958, 51638, '<td valign="top">Well, I see the ''white'', but I''m not sure it meets the challenge as well as it might.</td>', 'Well, I see the ''white'', but I''m not sure it meets the challenge as well as it might.', '2006-11-30 08:40:20.000000', NULL, 1),
(3074947, 431880, 51638, '<td valign="top">It seems to me that you''ve pushed the brightness way up to get the ''white'', but in the process have ended up with a very blown looking image.</td>', 'It seems to me that you''ve pushed the brightness way up to get the ''white'', but in the process have ended up with a very blown looking image.', '2006-11-30 08:43:06.000000', NULL, 1),
(3074951, 431790, 30049, '<td valign="top">This composition has nice balance to it, although I would have moved the cup left enough to cover the small gap at the bottom (edge of plate).  You did a good job with getting a good white background (not grey, yellow, etc... as many others struggled with).  Lighting is ok with the main source on the left.  Some bounce light from the other direction would help a little.  The reflections are somewhat distracting but can be tough to eliminate entirely (different camera angle, more white material in immediate surrounding, etc...).  Being that this is an advanced challenge with more liberal editing rules I would have applied a slight gaussian blur to the reflections, at least enough to not make it possible to see the camera, photographer, and doorway in the bottom left reflection.  :D  All of the above is JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.</td>', 'This composition has nice balance to it, although I would have moved the cup left enough to cover the small gap at the bottom (edge of plate).  You did a good job with getting a good white background (not grey, yellow, etc... as many others struggled with).  Lighting is ok with the main source on the left.  Some bounce light from the other direction would help a little.  The reflections are somewhat distracting but can be tough to eliminate entirely (different camera angle, more white material in immediate surrounding, etc...).  Being that this is an advanced challenge with more liberal editing rules I would have applied a slight gaussian blur to the reflections, at least enough to not make it possible to see the camera, photographer, and doorway in the bottom left reflection.  :D  All of the above is JMO of course.  Best of luck to you in the challenge.', '2006-11-30 08:45:18.000000', NULL, 1),
(3074952, 430896, 51638, '<td valign="top">Very nice work. I''d be surprised not to see this on the first page at the end of voting.</td>', 'Very nice work. I''d be surprised not to see this on the first page at the end of voting.', '2006-11-30 08:45:39.000000', NULL, 1),
(3074957, 431374, 51638, '<td valign="top">Sorry, but the background is far from being white.</td>', 'Sorry, but the background is far from being white.', '2006-11-30 08:49:19.000000', NULL, 1),
(3074964, 431934, 51638, '<td valign="top">You''ve managed to isolate the petals from the background, whilst still meeting the challenge perfectly. As a result this is one of the better flower images in this challenge. Well done.</td>', 'You''ve managed to isolate the petals from the background, whilst still meeting the challenge perfectly. As a result this is one of the better flower images in this challenge. Well done.', '2006-11-30 08:52:10.000000', NULL, 1),
