(3085427, 431870, 48389, '<td valign="top">As the girls already said, lovely holiday shot Jude! :o)</td>', 'As the girls already said, lovely holiday shot Jude! :o)', '2006-12-04 02:04:58.000000', NULL, 0),
(3085428, 431639, 30982, '<td valign="top">The detail here is exceptional - I like the way you can see all the little veins in the petals - you can see the softness!  You have a very good feel/sense for light.  The composition, as Ursula points out, is a bit lacking in that the flower is just kinda there.  Since I totally suck at shooting flowers, I can''t offer much help except to say see Ursula''s portfolio - she can shoot flowers.  With your ability to capture light, you''ll be able to work magic with shots like these!</td>', 'The detail here is exceptional - I like the way you can see all the little veins in the petals - you can see the softness!  You have a very good feel/sense for light.  The composition, as Ursula points out, is a bit lacking in that the flower is just kinda there.  Since I totally suck at shooting flowers, I can''t offer much help except to say see Ursula''s portfolio - she can shoot flowers.  With your ability to capture light, you''ll be able to work magic with shots like these!', '2006-12-04 02:05:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3085429, 431610, 66398, '<td valign="top">Wow. I''m surprised it wasn''t higher.  I mean 57 out of 233 isn''t bad but I thought it''d be in the top 10.  there were a lot of 5''s there and 9 votes below 4 sucks. This is an awesome photo!</td>', 'Wow. I''m surprised it wasn''t higher.  I mean 57 out of 233 isn''t bad but I thought it''d be in the top 10.  there were a lot of 5''s there and 9 votes below 4 sucks. This is an awesome photo!', '2006-12-04 02:05:09.000000', NULL, 0),
(3085430, 432076, 66097, '<td valign="top">x<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-04 02:09:34.</i></td>', 'x', '2006-12-04 02:05:53.000000', '2006-12-04 02:09:34.000000', 0),
(3085432, 432076, 66097, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by rlhcedar:</b></div><hr/><i> <i><b>A plastic "Woody"? That''s disgusting! Seriously, why not take a white egg? Also, your white balance is way off, overall the picture is much too dark.</b></i> commented by eyewave<br/>My husband threatened to throw this "PLASTIC" Woody away, then said, "I guess I''ll have to get you a new "REAL WOODY" for Christmas. So a real woody is on my Christmas list. Don''t suppose it will make my photos any better with the tremendously low scores I seem to continue to get. Even so, if I made one person laugh with this little set up then I accomplished the one thing I set out to do, against my husband warning that this will not help my average. The white balance is different platters with various shades of white.  Challenge did not say had to have a solid white or bright white background. <br/>Lesson learned, go with the flow if a previous challenge has set a precedent. <br/>side thought; Interesting to see so many bright on white and black on white scoring so well.<br/>second side thougth; There seems to be a few mean commenters out there, so my very sensitive side is being provoked to grow much stronger. Not that that is a bad thing. I just hope I do not become to mean in the process. </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-02-20 00:49:20.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by rlhcedar: A plastic "Woody"? That''s disgusting! Seriously, why not take a white egg? Also, your white balance is way off, overall the picture is much too dark. commented by eyewaveMy husband threatened to throw this "PLASTIC" Woody away, then said, "I guess I''ll have to get you a new "REAL WOODY" for Christmas. So a real woody is on my Christmas list. Don''t suppose it will make my photos any better with the tremendously low scores I seem to continue to get. Even so, if I made one person laugh with this little set up then I accomplished the one thing I set out to do, against my husband warning that this will not help my average. The white balance is different platters with various shades of white.  Challenge did not say had to have a solid white or bright white background. Lesson learned, go with the flow if a previous challenge has set a precedent. side thought; Interesting to see so many bright on white and black on white scoring so well.second side thougth; There seems to be a few mean commenters out there, so my very sensitive side is being provoked to grow much stronger. Not that that is a bad thing. I just hope I do not become to mean in the process. ', '2006-12-04 02:07:49.000000', '2007-02-20 00:49:20.000000', 0),
(3085438, 431727, 67145, '<td valign="top">i reckon this should have been in the top 10 ... guess you cant please everyone!!</td>', 'i reckon this should have been in the top 10 ... guess you cant please everyone!!', '2006-12-04 02:11:37.000000', NULL, 0),
(3085444, 431087, 48228, '<td valign="top">I also loved this one so much, and think it was by far, the best horse image in the challenge. Well done Sandy, and I know, and you know, that you also loved this one as well, and thats is also important.</td>', 'I also loved this one so much, and think it was by far, the best horse image in the challenge. Well done Sandy, and I know, and you know, that you also loved this one as well, and thats is also important.', '2006-12-04 02:15:32.000000', NULL, 0),
(3085447, 432049, 48228, '<td valign="top">Thank you Ursula, not only for your comment, but because it came from you, as it means such a lot to me, as I admire your work so much, and appriciate your knowledge as well. <br/>I was very pleased with this one myself, as I have no idea of how to do layers, which I love to learn about, so as to get the background whiter, as I would have liked it to be. <br/>I do like the softness of this one myself, so pleased with this result.<br/> <br/> <table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by ursula:</b></div><hr/><i> Ah, so this was yours.  I''m not good at telling who does which pictures :)  I love this one, Sherryl, it''s beautiful! </i></td></tr></table><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-04 03:15:55.</i></td>', 'Thank you Ursula, not only for your comment, but because it came from you, as it means such a lot to me, as I admire your work so much, and appriciate your knowledge as well. I was very pleased with this one myself, as I have no idea of how to do layers, which I love to learn about, so as to get the background whiter, as I would have liked it to be. I do like the softness of this one myself, so pleased with this result.  Originally posted by ursula: Ah, so this was yours.  I''m not good at telling who does which pictures :)  I love this one, Sherryl, it''s beautiful! ', '2006-12-04 02:18:20.000000', '2006-12-04 03:15:55.000000', 0),
(3085457, 431435, 48228, '<td valign="top">Perfection in everyway Ursula.....<br/>A stunning image, which the results show are what one deserves.....<br/>You have an amazing talant, and are so very gifted, especially in the processing that you do. <br/>It is always just so spot on, and never overdone.</td>', 'Perfection in everyway Ursula.....A stunning image, which the results show are what one deserves.....You have an amazing talant, and are so very gifted, especially in the processing that you do. It is always just so spot on, and never overdone.', '2006-12-04 02:26:07.000000', NULL, 0),
