(3087552, 430421, 60614, '<td valign="top">I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I did I would have given it a 6.  I loved the composition and the lighting was close to perfect.  It looks like the bottom left needed to be a bit more white.  Also, I looks like the aperture should have been set to f8 so all the dice would have been in focus more.  Still this was a great shot and should have done better.  Keep on shooting.</td>', 'I didn''t vote in this challenge but if I did I would have given it a 6.  I loved the composition and the lighting was close to perfect.  It looks like the bottom left needed to be a bit more white.  Also, I looks like the aperture should have been set to f8 so all the dice would have been in focus more.  Still this was a great shot and should have done better.  Keep on shooting.', '2006-12-04 20:44:22.000000', NULL, 0),
(3087565, 430896, 69454, '<td valign="top">THATS MY GRANDAUGHTER!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-04 20:48:19.</i></td>', 'THATS MY GRANDAUGHTER!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!!', '2006-12-04 20:47:47.000000', '2006-12-04 20:48:19.000000', 0),
(3087566, 432091, 32997, '<td valign="top">ok let''s be clear...this type of work hasn''t a chance in the DPC world...<br/>get your act together, find a girl, dress her in soft whites, and take a close-up...<br/> <br/>quite intriguing this feather caught by a thumb...really very original...and I can''t help thinking that it forces the viewer to think a little too much...why? does he hate birds? or is this someone who has recently broken up with his wife, and then realized he no longer needs to sleep with feather pillows...he holds this one last remnant of their relationship up to the sky, he is crying (thus the motion blur around the thumb)...<br/>you should consider doing a thumbscape series..really...just try to get the thumb not moving...(yeah I know, but c''mon look at your shutter speed...)...here comes the smiley...:)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-12-04 20:48:36.</i></td>', 'ok let''s be clear...this type of work hasn''t a chance in the DPC world...get your act together, find a girl, dress her in soft whites, and take a close-up... quite intriguing this feather caught by a thumb...really very original...and I can''t help thinking that it forces the viewer to think a little too much...why? does he hate birds? or is this someone who has recently broken up with his wife, and then realized he no longer needs to sleep with feather pillows...he holds this one last remnant of their relationship up to the sky, he is crying (thus the motion blur around the thumb)...you should consider doing a thumbscape series..really...just try to get the thumb not moving...(yeah I know, but c''mon look at your shutter speed...)...here comes the smiley...:)', '2006-12-04 20:47:49.000000', '2006-12-04 20:48:36.000000', 0),
