(3104991, 431720, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>WOW!  What a shot.  Certainly makes me look twice, that''s for sure.  The eyes are amazing!<br/> <br/>But, one of the other first things that jumped out at me were the hands.  They don''t look right for some reason.  I think it''s the position, it just doesn''t look natural to me overall.  The way that one set of fingers is curled and the other set is extended just seems a bit off to me for some reason.  And the shadow caused by the extended hand are also a bit distracting to me, just a bit.<br/> <br/>Other than that, this is a really amazing shot and very well done.  I love the composition of it and the look in her eyes is truely wonderful.<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! WOW!  What a shot.  Certainly makes me look twice, that''s for sure.  The eyes are amazing! But, one of the other first things that jumped out at me were the hands.  They don''t look right for some reason.  I think it''s the position, it just doesn''t look natural to me overall.  The way that one set of fingers is curled and the other set is extended just seems a bit off to me for some reason.  And the shadow caused by the extended hand are also a bit distracting to me, just a bit. Other than that, this is a really amazing shot and very well done.  I love the composition of it and the look in her eyes is truely wonderful. I hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges. Deannda', '2006-12-10 22:37:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3105005, 430421, 12448, '<td valign="top">Greetings from the Critique Club!<br/> <br/>What a cool shot.  When I first glanced at it I thought I was looking at some really neat ice cubes with some coloring in then but then realized it was just colored dice, but cool all the same.<br/> <br/>Nice shot in that you have your focus and the detail shown is really nice.<br/> <br/>But, the first feeling I get from this shot after looking at it is that the dice are begging to be set free.  Reading your comments I realized you are very limited on just how much space you can put around them but even on a washing machine, unless it''s a tiny apartment size one, you should be able to add a little more space around the subject.  This will bring more lightness into the overall shot and possibly bring better composition to the shot.<br/> <br/>The color on the dice probably hurt you in the end, while not solid colors it is still very dark compared to the white of the machine.<br/> <br/>Looking at your profile and portfolio you have some really nice work and a great eye.  I hope to see more of your work soon!<br/> <br/>I hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges.<br/> <br/>Deannda</td>', 'Greetings from the Critique Club! What a cool shot.  When I first glanced at it I thought I was looking at some really neat ice cubes with some coloring in then but then realized it was just colored dice, but cool all the same. Nice shot in that you have your focus and the detail shown is really nice. But, the first feeling I get from this shot after looking at it is that the dice are begging to be set free.  Reading your comments I realized you are very limited on just how much space you can put around them but even on a washing machine, unless it''s a tiny apartment size one, you should be able to add a little more space around the subject.  This will bring more lightness into the overall shot and possibly bring better composition to the shot. The color on the dice probably hurt you in the end, while not solid colors it is still very dark compared to the white of the machine. Looking at your profile and portfolio you have some really nice work and a great eye.  I hope to see more of your work soon! I hope my comments help and good luck in future challenges. Deannda', '2006-12-10 22:49:41.000000', NULL, 0),
